You had nothing on Elbereth and not much on scare monster, 
so might I suggest:

HOW TO GET MONSTERS TO LEAVE YOU ALONE

There are two methods beyond running away: engraving Elbereth and a scroll
of scare monster.

Engraving Elbereth:

You can write this in the dust with your fingers (E-) and non-@ monsters
will not hit you although they may throw things at you. If you swing at
them or throw things at them you will scuff out the engraving.
It will fade out eventually and they will hit again.

If you levitate above the engraving you cannot scuff it out.

If you engrave with a weapon it will be dulled unless it is an athame.
Wizards start with athames. Elbereth engraved with a weapon doesn't fade
out and doesn't scuff out if you fight.

Scare monster:

If you drop it and step on it, it is like a permanent Elbereth: you can
fight all you want without them ever hitting back. If you drop it in a
corridor they will not cross it.

Every time you drop/pick up a scroll of scare monster it moves toward
a cursed state. Drop a blessed scroll, pick it up it is uncursed. Drop
that uncursed scroll, pick it up it is cursed. Drop that cursed scroll,
pick it up it turns to dust. If you pick up a scroll that turns to dust
it is a worn out scare monster scroll.

If you read it, monsters in the room will leave but it is a real waste to
read it.

Just my 2 zorkmids,
